      "avalancheActivity": {
        "comment": "In steep rocky terrain and on extremely steep slopes small and medium sized avalanches are to be expected as the day progresses. Above approximately 2300 m they can be triggered in the new snow and wind slab layers and reach large size in some cases. Individual gliding avalanches can also occur. <br/> <br/> The wind slabs of the last few days can be released by a single winter sport participant in isolated cases in particular on very steep northeast, east and south facing slopes at high altitude. They will be covered with new snow and therefore difficult to recognise. Adjacent to ridgelines and in gullies and bowls and at the base of rock walls the likelihood of avalanches is higher.",
