      "snowpackStructure": {
        "comment": "20 to 30 cm of snow will fall until Wednesday above approximately 1200 m. <br/> As a consequence of new snow and a sometimes moderate southeasterly wind, soft wind slabs will form by the evening adjacent to ridgelines. <br/> As a consequence of the occasionally strong northwesterly wind, snow drift accumulations formed at the weekend. <br/> Above approximately 2200 m there are 60 to 130 cm of snow, and even as much as 190 cm in some localities, especially above approximately 2500 m. <br/> The snowpack will be in some cases unstable. Towards its base, the snowpack is moist, in particular below approximately 2500 m. <br/> The Avalanche Warning Service currently has only a small amount of information that has been collected in the field."
      },
