        "comment": "10 to 20 cm of snow, and up to 30 cm in some localities, will fall until the evening above approximately 1000 m. <br/> As a consequence of the moderate to strong southeasterly wind, fresh snow drift accumulations will form in the course of the day. <br/> Above approximately 2000 m there are 30 to 60 cm of snow, and even more in some localities. <br/> The snowpack will become in some cases unstable. <br/> Towards its base, the snowpack is moist, in particular below approximately 2500 m. <br/> At low and intermediate altitudes only a little snow is lying. <br/> The Avalanche Warning Service currently has only a small amount of information that has been collected in the field."
